==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɑntɪŋ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɒntɪŋ/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-wanting.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒntɪŋ|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|wantyng}}, {{m|enm|wantynge}}, {{m|enm|wantand}}, equivalent to {{af|en|want|-ing|id2=participial}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# That [[want]]s or desires.
# [[absent|Absent]] or [[lacking]].
#* {{RQ:Addison Cato|1|text=Already ''Cæſar''<br>Has ravaged more than half the Globe, and ſees<br>Mankind grown thin by his deſtructive Sword:<br>Should he go further, Numbers would be '''wanting'''<br>To form new Battels, and ſupport his Crimes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1813|author=Jane Austen|title=Pride and Prejudice|publisher=Modern Library Edition|year_published=1995|page=171
|passage={{...}} but where other powers of entertainment are '''wanting''', the true philosopher will derive benefit from such as are given.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1902|publisher=United States National Museum|title=Proceedings: Entomological papers|volume=25-26|page=201
|passage=Discal black dot small or '''wanting'''. Transverse posterior line reduced to two dotlets or altogether '''wanting'''.}}
# [[deficient|Deficient]].

